@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# AutoVideoAI v7.0.76: Gemini Web hooks
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Hooks are drafted by Gemini Web** after the narration words and text cards are ready. The
+  draft runs in the prepare stage and is saved to `production/hooks.json`. The raw reply is kept in
+  `production/hooks-draft.json`.
+- **Opt-in.** Create has a new checkbox, "Add Gemini Web hooks where the narration needs them".
+  It is off by default and needs a voiceover. The setting is `hooks_enabled`.
+- **Limits.** At most 6 hooks. Each is at most 60 characters on one line. Each is shown for
+  2.5 to 3.5 seconds (3.0 seconds by default, clipped at the end of the video). Hooks are at least
+  10 seconds apart. Each is anchored to a spoken word, so it appears when the narrator reaches that
+  moment.
+- **Placement.** A hook is a pop pill near the top centre of the frame. A hook that would cover a
+  text card, a points series or any other non-watermark overlay is dropped and logged as
+  `hooks_dropped_overlap`.
+- **Failure handling.** If Gemini Web is not signed in or returns an invalid draft, the job logs
+  `hooks_skipped` and continues without hooks. The render also logs `hooks_render_skipped` and
+  continues if the saved hooks no longer match the narration.
+- **Staleness.** Hooks are cached by a fingerprint over the voice audio, the words, the script,
+  the topic and the language. If any of these change, the saved hooks are refused until the
+  job is resumed and hooks are redrafted.
+
+## Files
+
+- `engine/video_hooks.py`: prompt, validation, drafting, cache, render-time placement.
+- `engine/render/hook_cards.py`: pill PNG renderer (fits text to two lines, portrait and landscape).
+- `engine/factory.py`: draft step after speech cards; overlay step before `graphics_plan.json` is saved.
+- `engine/studio_config.py`, `app.py`: `hooks_enabled` setting and checkbox.
+- `tests/test_v776_hooks.py`: 23 offline tests.
+
+## Install
+
+Install from 7.0.75 with `tools/update_v775_to_v776.py` (dry run first, then `--apply`). Stop the
+dashboard before `--apply`. Outputs, saved jobs and browser profiles are never touched.
+
+## Not yet verified
+
+- A live Gemini Web hook draft has not been run in this build.
+- A full job render with hooks on the user's footage has not been run.
